<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bahlul Lodi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1451–<a href="/years/1489">1489</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Bahlul · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bahlul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi</a> was an Afghan noble who founded the Lodi dynasty, the last ruling house of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>, taking power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in 1451. He restored some of the sultanate's authority in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, notably by conquering the Sharqi sultanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaunpur">Jaunpur</a>. His dynasty was ended by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a> at Panipat in 1526.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bahlul-lodi.jpg" alt="Bahlul Lodi" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Drnsreedhar1959 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Bahlul_Lodi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Lodi recovery under <b>Bahlul</b> and Sikandar was genuine but limited.</blockquote><a href="/empire/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Husain Shah Sharqi's repeated attacks on Delhi failed, and <b>Bahlul Lodi</b> conquered Jaunpur in 1479.</blockquote><a href="/state/jaunpur-sultanate">Jaunpur Sultanate</a></li><li><blockquote>Husain Shah Langah, the most important ruler, reigned for about three decades, repelled attacks from <b>Bahlul Lodi</b> of Delhi and expanded towards Sindh and the Indus frontier.</blockquote><a href="/state/langah-sultanate">Langah Sultanate</a></li><li><blockquote>Tradition holds that the Sufi Shaikh Sadruddin Sadr-i-Jahan, of Sherwani Afghan descent, settled in the area in 1454 and married a daughter of <b>Bahlul Lodi</b>, receiving land grants.</blockquote><a href="/state/malerkotla-state">Malerkotla State</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=28.67,77.22&amp;year=1470" aria-label="Delhi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6568 1115 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Bahlul Lodi"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7018 1385h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7018 1385h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=28.67,77.22&amp;year=1470">What was here in 1470? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
